Terminology
\layout Standard

A 
\emph on 
session
\emph default 
 is a series of interactions between two users.
 The interactions themselves consist of 
\emph on 
messages
\emph default 
 each of which may be split into 
\emph on 
packets
\emph default 
.
 
\layout Standard

One example of a session would be this lecture.
 The session consists of a mainly one-way communication between me, the
 server, and you multiple clients.
 In this case most of the information transfer is one-way with me sending
 a series of messages, each involving a different subject: My Identity,
 The History of Communication, this courses subject matter etc.
 and you acknowledging by your lively reactions.
 Each message consists of a series of packets, in this case perhaps the
 sentences that I speak.
 The communication medium is the air between us.
 
